From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Wed, 29 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] drm/msm/dsi: log the bonded command link checks

The bonded transaction validates two things before it touches hardware:
that a master link is known, and that the link the command came from is
that master.  Only the second one says why it failed; the first one, and
the case where the peer host is not up yet, still return a bare -EINVAL
or -ENODEV, which is the same complaint this series set out to remove,
just one branch further up.

Report both through the device that issued the command, naming the link
ids, and keep the error codes as they are.  Nothing else changes: the
checks stay ahead of the prepare step, so a rejected call still leaves
both links untouched.

Signed-off-by: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
index 3fa1a7b23..a5875e725 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_manager.c
@@ -636,8 +636,12 @@ static int dsi_mgr_bonded_cmd_xfer(int id, const struct mipi_dsi_msg *msg)
 	const struct msm_dsi_host_cfg_ops *ops;
 	int master_id = dsi_mgr_bonded_master_link_id(id);
 
-	if (master_id < 0 || master_id >= DSI_MAX)
+	if (master_id < 0 || master_id >= DSI_MAX) {
+		dev_err(&dsi_mgr_get_dsi(id)->pdev->dev,
+			"bonded command on link %d, but no valid master link is known (%d)\n",
+			id, master_id);
 		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * Only the master link owns the broadcast engine and its completion
@@ -655,8 +659,12 @@ static int dsi_mgr_bonded_cmd_xfer(int id, const struct mipi_dsi_msg *msg)
 
 	master_dsi = dsi_mgr_get_dsi(master_id);
 	slave_dsi = dsi_mgr_get_other_dsi(master_id);
-	if (!master_dsi || !slave_dsi || !master_dsi->host || !slave_dsi->host)
+	if (!master_dsi || !slave_dsi || !master_dsi->host || !slave_dsi->host) {
+		dev_err(&dsi_mgr_get_dsi(id)->pdev->dev,
+			"bonded command on link %d, but master link %d is not ready\n",
+			id, master_id);
 		return -ENODEV;
+	}
 
 	/* Which hosts run the broadcast engine is per-generation knowledge. */
 	ops = msm_dsi_host_get_cfg_ops(master_dsi->host);

